WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.325 --> 00:00:07.433
[Subtitles by danielsangeo]

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:09.815
Yep.

00:00:11.067 --> 00:00:13.933
Hello! Everything's still radioactive!

00:00:13.933 --> 00:00:18.000
Whatever it is I'm NOT doing
needs to ESPECIALLY not be here!

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:21.233
I think this is the end of
the voyage of the swamp boat.

00:00:21.233 --> 00:00:26.267
God, look at that. Even if this wasn't
radioactive, why would I want to be here?

00:00:26.267 --> 00:00:28.167
Oh, more of those missiles, huh?

00:00:28.167 --> 00:00:30.233
So were they aiming for me specifically,

00:00:30.233 --> 00:00:35.300
or just decided, y'know what? Let's make
sure no one ever wants to live on Earth?

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:37.367
It looks like there's houses nearby here,

00:00:37.367 --> 00:00:40.700
why would--Burke! That the
name of the "Aliens" guy.

00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:43.100
Dammit, Burke! You screwed all of us!

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:45.367
You're not real and it didn't even matter!

00:00:45.367 --> 00:00:46.867
Oh, it's a gate.

00:00:46.867 --> 00:00:48.467
Okay, I can do this.

00:00:48.467 --> 00:00:49.300
[headcrab chirp]

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:51.933
What was that?! I know I heard it...

00:00:53.433 --> 00:00:55.200
They're out there...

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:56.767
[headcrab chirp]
Well, I don't SEE them,

00:00:56.767 --> 00:01:00.533
so I wish they would stop making noises
so I can pretend they don't exist.

00:01:00.533 --> 00:01:03.100
[straining]
All right... Let's get you up there...

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:04.267
[straining]
Come...ON...

00:01:04.267 --> 00:01:06.800
[straining]
God...dyah...SYAAAAHHH! GYAH!

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:10.867
[exhaling, gibbering]

00:01:10.867 --> 00:01:16.067
Y'know, once again, I'm lucky I'm me,
because anybody else would be dead by now.

00:01:16.067 --> 00:01:20.267
This isn't an underground railroad
anymore. This is a slaughterhouse.

00:01:20.267 --> 00:01:24.400
Even if the cops weren't gunning
down everyone--which is a big "if"--

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:28.123
if I wasn't me, I should've
died back in that scrapyard.

00:01:28.123 --> 00:01:31.833
That thing was BUILT to kill
people. That's its only purpose.

00:01:31.833 --> 00:01:35.800
Even now, the jury's still out
with this radiation. Dammit!

00:01:35.800 --> 00:01:39.300
At least when I'm being shot at,
I know if I'd been shot or not.

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:41.533
Gamma rays keep you guessing.

00:01:41.533 --> 00:01:44.067
Y'know, I'm starting to think
this isn't a coincidence.

00:01:44.067 --> 00:01:46.600
This route couldn't be more dangerous.

00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:48.200
Is this on purpose?

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:50.533
People think--Whoa... Easy...

00:01:50.533 --> 00:01:53.333
People think they're escaping
and joining the underground,

00:01:53.333 --> 00:01:55.400
when really, it's all just a giant mouse trap

00:01:55.400 --> 00:01:57.933
to catch dissidents that
slip through the cracks.

00:01:57.933 --> 00:02:02.233
This just got even more "Nineteen Eighty-Four"
than it was already. What year is it?

00:02:02.233 --> 00:02:03.415
Oh, shit!

00:02:03.415 --> 00:02:03.900
Oof!

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:06.767
Good seat padding.

00:02:06.767 --> 00:02:11.333
But wait, if this is just a meat
grinder, why is the CIA involved?

00:02:11.333 --> 00:02:14.993
Why are they growing a resistance if
the plan is to kill them all anyway?

00:02:14.993 --> 00:02:17.867
Maybe it's a little bit of Column
A, and a little bit of Column B.

00:02:17.867 --> 00:02:20.800
I guess it gets boring playing
with people's lives all day.

00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:22.300
I'm just going to ram this.

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:23.567
This is a bad idea...!

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:26.100
[spitting]

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:27.167
Not that bad.

00:02:27.167 --> 00:02:31.067
OH! SPEAK OF THE DEVIL! WE NEED TO TALK!

00:02:31.067 --> 00:02:33.300
I KNOW WHAT YOU GUYS DID IN NICARAGUA!

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:38.767
Yeah, pull in here. It's about fucking time!

00:02:38.767 --> 00:02:41.400
I've been hanging out in the wind here!

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:44.164
I cannot wait to hear his explanation.

00:02:44.164 --> 00:02:48.567
I mean, it's probably going to be bullshit,
but what can you even say at this point?

00:02:48.567 --> 00:02:50.400
"Oh yeah, we went and--" ...what?

00:02:51.133 --> 00:02:52.100
OOF!

00:02:52.100 --> 00:02:53.000
[screaming]

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:54.200
[underwater screaming]

00:02:56.533 --> 00:02:58.333
WHAT THE FUCK?!

00:02:58.333 --> 00:02:59.233
What...?

00:02:59.233 --> 00:03:01.567
Did he get eaten by the zombies?!

00:03:01.567 --> 00:03:05.367
I JUST saw him! That was really fast!

00:03:05.367 --> 00:03:06.700
No...

00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:09.133
No, come on. I didn't see a body.

00:03:09.133 --> 00:03:12.667
I mean, I'm stranded here
without him, so that's nice!

00:03:12.667 --> 00:03:17.033
Did the master of space and time really
just get his head bitten off by a zombie?

00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:21.733
Oh, it backed off? They're getting smarter.

00:03:21.733 --> 00:03:22.233
Great...

00:03:22.867 --> 00:03:25.067
Okay. What'd you do with him?

00:03:26.333 --> 00:03:28.567
Not the answer I was hoping for.

00:03:28.567 --> 00:03:31.200
Well, it's not them. He was wearing a suit.

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:35.167
Oh, this is recent! This must've
happened, what, twenty minutes ago?

00:03:35.167 --> 00:03:36.300
RADIO: Station 12, come in.

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:37.233
What?

00:03:37.233 --> 00:03:39.020
RADIO: Station 12, do you read?

00:03:39.020 --> 00:03:42.433
Uh, yeah, this is Station 12?

00:03:42.433 --> 00:03:44.500
[radio static]
Ah, shit. I hit the wrong button.

00:03:44.500 --> 00:03:45.067
How do I...?

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:50.700
Fuck it. This isn't worth my time. The
spook is who I need to be looking for.

00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:54.567
So he didn't come through here; did
he go around the back? I didn't check.

00:03:54.567 --> 00:03:56.967
No, he'd have to shimmy along the fence.

00:03:56.967 --> 00:03:59.533
He didn't seem like the type
to want to get his suit dirty.

00:03:59.533 --> 00:04:01.267
Oh, did he climb up here?

00:04:01.267 --> 00:04:04.867
He had to do SOMETHING
unless these are HIS zombies.

00:04:04.867 --> 00:04:08.333
Which... Well, I don't know
if I want to go there yet.

00:04:08.333 --> 00:04:11.167
Oh what? He's in the crawlspace?
No, no one's up here.

00:04:11.167 --> 00:04:12.733
[growls]

00:04:12.733 --> 00:04:14.333
Oh, there's something around back.

00:04:14.333 --> 00:04:17.833
Oh, okay. So he was just flagging
me? Meet him in the back?

00:04:19.465 --> 00:04:20.933
Yeah, there we go.

00:04:22.750 --> 00:04:24.633
He must have a secret entrance.

00:04:25.267 --> 00:04:26.392
Yeah...

00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:29.500
I can see that.

00:04:29.500 --> 00:04:32.733
Meeting in the old barn isn't
clandestine enough for him.

00:04:32.733 --> 00:04:36.633
He's got to meet in the house
out back BEHIND the old barn.

00:04:36.633 --> 00:04:38.467
I mean, he has to be around here somewhere;

00:04:38.467 --> 00:04:41.133
why would he signal me if he
didn't want me to come up here?

00:04:41.133 --> 00:04:45.100
Y'know, I think I'm starting to get
why he dropped me off the way he did.

00:04:45.100 --> 00:04:48.467
It's really stupid,
but I think I get it now.

00:04:48.467 --> 00:04:50.233
What's happening... Okay.

00:04:51.800 --> 00:04:53.967
Uh... What?

00:04:53.967 --> 00:04:55.367
Was that a trap?

00:04:55.367 --> 00:04:57.933
Well, that would freak me
out if it fell on my head.

00:04:57.933 --> 00:05:01.567
Oh. This is where people come to drink bleach.

00:05:01.567 --> 00:05:03.233
All right, not here.

00:05:03.233 --> 00:05:06.300
But yeah, what's happening
is he thinks he's Mr. Miyagi,

00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:11.000
and serving me up to the police is his
interpretation of "wax on, wax off",

00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:16.733
because apparently surviving Black Mesa and
an ALIEN WORLD means I need to prove myself.

00:05:16.733 --> 00:05:20.100
A-HA! Really? Nothing?

00:05:20.100 --> 00:05:23.100
Oh, beer! THERE'S the silver lining.

00:05:23.100 --> 00:05:24.067
EMPTY!

00:05:24.067 --> 00:05:24.733
[growls]

00:05:24.733 --> 00:05:28.500
He's really not here?
Dammit, I'm not used to this.

00:05:28.500 --> 00:05:30.433
I'm observing mounting evidence,

00:05:30.433 --> 00:05:34.667
yet somehow it's not narrowing down my
theories as to what's happening at all.

00:05:34.667 --> 00:05:37.900
The only thing I can conclude
so far is that he's an asshole.

00:05:37.900 --> 00:05:40.167
I don't need a doctorate for that one.

00:05:40.167 --> 00:05:43.633
So I guess he's gone. Fine, I'm gone, too.

00:05:44.900 --> 00:05:48.600
He probably just hit a button on his
watch and teleported out of there.

00:05:49.733 --> 00:05:54.633
Wait, no. He didn't even hit a button,
did he? I was there. He just did it.

00:05:54.633 --> 00:05:56.633
Well, not that way.

00:05:56.633 --> 00:06:00.867
Y'know that kind of pisses
me off--okay, let's go--

00:06:00.867 --> 00:06:04.200
because he's not smarter
than me, I mean, come on,

00:06:04.200 --> 00:06:06.500
but he DOES have better technology.

00:06:06.500 --> 00:06:10.667
We were doing groundbreaking work and
he just teleports in like it's nothing.

00:06:10.667 --> 00:06:14.733
That would be like if we were in the 1800s
inventing the internal combustion engine,

00:06:14.733 --> 00:06:18.867
and he just shows up in a Ferrari
doing donuts outside our workshop.

00:06:18.867 --> 00:06:20.833
That's really demoralizing.

00:06:20.833 --> 00:06:22.200
This another dead end?

00:06:22.200 --> 00:06:23.867
Oh no. There's a ramp.

00:06:23.867 --> 00:06:28.100
I'm doing it. This is the most fun I'm
going to have for a while, I know it.

00:06:28.100 --> 00:06:28.867
Whoo-hoo!

00:06:28.867 --> 00:06:30.267
Oh, shit!

00:06:30.267 --> 00:06:31.200
OOF!

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:33.000
I almost rolled the boat!

00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:34.333
Well, I didn't.

00:06:34.333 --> 00:06:37.633
Okay, so, dead end and...

00:06:37.633 --> 00:06:38.800
dead end.

00:06:38.800 --> 00:06:41.167
Aw man. It's those photo bots.

00:06:41.167 --> 00:06:44.767
I'd love to imagine future people take
these along with them on fishing trips

00:06:44.767 --> 00:06:46.633
and that's all this is, but no.

00:06:47.467 --> 00:06:48.900
You're not a bass-finder.

00:06:50.333 --> 00:06:52.500
[robotic chirping]

00:06:52.500 --> 00:06:52.933
No.

00:06:54.733 --> 00:06:58.167
You made a compelling case,
but my verdict still stands.

00:06:58.167 --> 00:07:00.967
I haven't seen one fisherman
since I got here,

00:07:00.967 --> 00:07:04.000
and you know what?
I don't think I'm going to.

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:07.767
Something's wrong if somebody
is fishing in this river.

00:07:07.767 --> 00:07:13.433
Yeah, "river". I'm really questioning the
wisdom of taking a boat down this "river".

00:07:13.433 --> 00:07:14.867
It would've been better off if we had--

00:07:14.867 --> 00:07:17.100
REBEL: Hey down there! Supplies!

00:07:17.100 --> 00:07:20.133
Yeah, supplies! I like supplies!

00:07:20.133 --> 00:07:21.307
REBEL: Look out below!

00:07:21.307 --> 00:07:22.433
Three o'clock!

00:07:22.433 --> 00:07:24.367
Oh wait, that would be my three...

00:07:24.367 --> 00:07:26.200
Actually, it's my one o'clock...

00:07:26.200 --> 00:07:28.233
Your nine--ah, you figured it out.

00:07:28.233 --> 00:07:30.900
Okay, so what do we have here?

00:07:30.900 --> 00:07:32.933
Maybe some REAL beer this time.

00:07:33.867 --> 00:07:35.533
Find out in a minute.

00:07:35.533 --> 00:07:38.400
Bullets. I'm surprised that floats.

00:07:38.400 --> 00:07:40.567
And let me guess. Bullets.

00:07:41.433 --> 00:07:44.767
Nothing. Okay, well, one out of two.

00:07:44.767 --> 00:07:47.567
Oh, this isn't for you, but
I have something for you.

00:07:48.767 --> 00:07:49.833
If you hold still...

00:07:51.533 --> 00:07:54.900
Y'know, the bullets were for me, but
all I'm doing is giving them to you.

00:07:54.900 --> 00:07:58.400
I may as well just be the middleman.
You're the winner in all this.

00:07:58.400 --> 00:08:00.067
You don't even need a boat.

00:08:00.067 --> 00:08:02.000
Well, you do now.

00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:03.067
Nyah...

00:08:03.067 --> 00:08:03.933
That's better.

00:08:03.933 --> 00:08:06.900
Okay, this really IS looking
like the end of the line.

00:08:06.900 --> 00:08:11.500
I'm obviously going the right way; Santa's
little helper there had a package for me.

00:08:11.500 --> 00:08:14.867
Clearly I'm the first person
to come through here by boat,

00:08:14.867 --> 00:08:17.800
or else it's been a long
time since someone else has.

00:08:17.800 --> 00:08:22.233
I mean, what is this? A collapsed
bridge? Some sort of junkyard ramp?

00:08:22.233 --> 00:08:24.900
Can I move this? Why doesn't it connect?

00:08:26.267 --> 00:08:26.967
[metal groaning]

00:08:26.967 --> 00:08:27.900
I heard something.

00:08:29.167 --> 00:08:32.800
Okay, this underground railroad
is completely compromised then.

00:08:32.800 --> 00:08:35.267
If people aren't being
outright sent to their deaths,

00:08:35.267 --> 00:08:39.400
then the paths lead nowhere because all
the information is hopelessly outdated.

00:08:39.400 --> 00:08:41.700
Why? They have radio.

00:08:41.700 --> 00:08:46.300
...they HAD radio. I guess radio
doesn't help much if everybody's dead.

00:08:46.300 --> 00:08:49.833
"Where are you? Please respond. Hello?"

00:08:49.833 --> 00:08:53.167
Oh wait. The ramp's propped
up by the barrel? That's odd.

00:08:53.167 --> 00:08:56.033
So if I prop it up more, what, I jump it?

00:08:56.033 --> 00:08:58.400
This is stupid. Let's try it.

00:09:00.933 --> 00:09:01.700
[underwater mm-hmm]

00:09:06.967 --> 00:09:10.167
[underwater straining]

00:09:10.167 --> 00:09:11.833
[underwater mumbling]

00:09:13.267 --> 00:09:17.867
That doesn't look like it did
much. This boat was a mistake.

00:09:17.867 --> 00:09:21.067
Yeah, this is a joke. That's
how I know this was the plan.

00:09:21.067 --> 00:09:23.133
I'm looking at the official plan.

00:09:23.133 --> 00:09:25.633
Some stoner thought this up, thinking,

00:09:25.633 --> 00:09:31.200
"Yeah! It'll be like Evel Knievel,
except, like, on the water, man!"

00:09:31.200 --> 00:09:32.400
[inhale]

00:09:32.400 --> 00:09:36.400
Lambda. Oh my God. Is that what this is?

00:09:36.400 --> 00:09:38.467
That's the sign of the railroad.

00:09:38.467 --> 00:09:40.200
Fine! This way!

00:09:40.200 --> 00:09:43.033
So no one thought to tell me
THAT'S the sign to follow?

00:09:43.033 --> 00:09:44.867
That wouldn't make my life easier?

00:09:44.867 --> 00:09:46.967
And isn't that a little obvious?

00:09:46.967 --> 00:09:48.800
If I can figure that out by accident,

00:09:48.800 --> 00:09:51.967
what do they think the cops
LOOKING for them are going to do?

00:09:51.967 --> 00:09:56.900
Although--dead end--to give them
credit, these cops aren't that bright.

00:09:56.900 --> 00:10:00.100
But I don't know. They could
maybe figure that one out.

00:10:00.100 --> 00:10:01.933
Oh, more of these canisters, huh?

00:10:01.933 --> 00:10:06.567
I would say I'm barking up the wrong tree,
but this is obviously what they had in mind.

00:10:06.567 --> 00:10:08.200
These are not smart people.

00:10:09.300 --> 00:10:13.133
Well, you know what? I'm up here.
I think it's time to abandon ship.

00:10:13.133 --> 00:10:16.367
I mean, maybe if there was
WATER, I would reconsider,

00:10:16.367 --> 00:10:19.867
but I don't think this is any faster
than going on foot at this point.

00:10:19.867 --> 00:10:22.867
Jesus Christ, look at this...

00:10:22.867 --> 00:10:25.800
So it's THIS, or try my
luck on the countryside

00:10:25.800 --> 00:10:27.700
where aliens have implanted in the ground

00:10:27.700 --> 00:10:30.600
to come jump up and--
Okay, I'll try the boat.

00:10:30.600 --> 00:10:33.533
That's a false choice anyway
because this isn't going to work,

00:10:33.533 --> 00:10:36.429
but this will only take five
minutes; let's prove it anyway.

00:10:40.133 --> 00:10:41.333
Yeah, I forget...

00:10:43.733 --> 00:10:45.800
[underwater grunting]

00:10:48.100 --> 00:10:53.333
It's a luxury being able to test
your hypothesis. It's been so long.

00:10:55.200 --> 00:10:56.767
[underwater grunting]

00:11:02.167 --> 00:11:03.633
Yeah, this isn't going to work.

00:11:03.633 --> 00:11:06.467
I'm probably on my way to meeting
a bunch of skeletons anyway.

00:11:06.467 --> 00:11:10.667
They already know this path. They hit
that barn dead center with the missile.

00:11:10.667 --> 00:11:14.367
So either they know about the lambda
sign, they're monitoring the radio,

00:11:14.367 --> 00:11:17.567
or they have a mole. Or, you
know what? All the above.

00:11:17.567 --> 00:11:22.333
Eh, I think that first ramp's going to
slow me down on the second one. Hm...

00:11:22.333 --> 00:11:26.367
Or maybe they just did the classic
technique: Capture somebody and torture them.

00:11:26.367 --> 00:11:27.867
I've got to clear this.

00:11:27.867 --> 00:11:30.433
That was easy. C'mon. Get out of there!

00:11:30.433 --> 00:11:31.300
Ow!

00:11:31.300 --> 00:11:32.700
STOP BEING WOOD!

00:11:32.700 --> 00:11:35.433
I don't need you jamming
up the--Okay, that's good.

00:11:35.433 --> 00:11:37.600
Yeah, I wouldn't hold up under torture.

00:11:37.600 --> 00:11:41.167
That's why it's so stupid
sending me here the way they did.

00:11:41.167 --> 00:11:41.733
I mean...

00:11:42.900 --> 00:11:45.900
He all but delivered me to the authorities.

00:11:45.900 --> 00:11:49.133
They had me dead to rights
at the train station.

00:11:49.133 --> 00:11:53.067
If that Barney guy had been taking a
smoke break, I'd be a cell right now

00:11:53.067 --> 00:11:57.733
and they'd probably be using me to develop
a weapon or better teleporters for THEM.

00:11:57.733 --> 00:12:01.133
I mean, I'm not a collaborator,
trying to sell out my own species,

00:12:01.133 --> 00:12:05.733
but you introduce me to the torture chair,
and hey! Guess what? I'm a collaborator now.

00:12:05.733 --> 00:12:07.500
Okay, Control. We are ready for takeoff.

00:12:07.500 --> 00:12:11.133
We are proceeding down the runway.
Speed is good. We are in our lane.

00:12:11.133 --> 00:12:12.567
WE HAVE SOME TURBULENCE!

00:12:12.567 --> 00:12:13.633
Ah-AH-AH!

00:12:13.633 --> 00:12:14.233
OOF!

00:12:14.233 --> 00:12:15.867
MAYDAY! MAYDAY!

00:12:15.867 --> 00:12:16.967
WAAAAH!

00:12:16.967 --> 00:12:19.900
Pluh! Belay that. No mayday.

00:12:19.900 --> 00:12:22.001
This just...sucks...

00:12:24.500 --> 00:12:26.633
Didn't they have this problem
in a Charlie Brown movie

00:12:26.633 --> 00:12:29.600
where they're stuck on a river?
How'd they get out of that?

00:12:30.600 --> 00:12:34.967
I think Snoopy rescued them with a
bulldozer. That doesn't help me at all.

